-- title:
--   Generic point of an irreducible smooth special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, and let $\varpi \in R$ be such that the maximal ideal of $R$ equals the ideal generated by $\varpi$. Let $X$ be a scheme (in the bottom universe) and $f : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a smooth morphism, and assume that the topological preimage under $f$ of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, i.e. the underlying space of the special fibre, is irreducible. Then there exists a point $\xi \in X$ with $f(\xi)$ equal to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ such that: (i) every irreducible component $Z$ of the subspace $\{x \in X : f(x) = \text{closed point}\}$ contains a point whose underlying point of $X$ is $\xi$; and (ii) the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$ is a domain and, with this domain structure, a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the single element obtained as the germ at $\xi$ of the global section $f^{\ast}\varpi$, that is, the image of $\varpi$ under the inverse of the canonical isomorphism $R \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R, \mathcal{O})$ followed by the map on global sections induced by $f$, and then by the germ map $\Gamma(X,\mathcal{O}_X) \to \mathcal{O}_{X,\xi}$.
--
--   This identifies the generic point of the special fibre of a smooth scheme over a discrete valuation ring as a point of codimension one at which the local ring is again a discrete valuation ring, with the pullback of a uniformiser of the base as uniformiser. It is used in the comparison of invertible modules over a scheme smooth over a discrete valuation ring with their pullbacks, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.nonempty_iso_of_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible.nonempty_iso_of_nonempty_pullback_iso_of_isDiscreteValuationRing).
